  "notes": "Refugee Camp / Booga Basement into Platinum Sound — live-bass, Caribbean-inflected R&B crossover, 1996–2008; the research combines them into one entry \"because their production credits are effectively inseparable across this window\", and that decision is carried here. The band is \"87–100 straight (backbeat 2&4), with one-drop and 4/4-reggae variants\", mode 91. Three drum deltas: \"kick on 1 with a one-drop variant putting the kick on beat 3\" — so the kick anchors on both 1 and 3, which nothing else in this section does for that reason; \"snare/rim flat on 2&4\" with a rimshot layer pushed 5–11 ms; and \"live hand percussion (congas, timbales) layered over a programmed base; the feel is played rather than gridded\" — a five-lane conga/timbale/bongo/shaker/cowbell bed at four to eight hits a bar with `quantizeStrength` at 0.56 and `velocityVar` 0.28. The identifying parameter is stated as a superlative: \"**the bass is the identity** — Duplessis is a bassist from age 14 (influences Aston 'Family Man' Barrett and James Jamerson) and plays the parts himself: melodic, walking, reggae-derived lines that carry the harmony, mixed forward, with no 808 sub\". So `followRootsProb` is 0.3 — the lowest bass root-follow in this whole section — with a seven-wide passing-tone set, `anticipationProb` 0.52 and four walking cell shapes, and there is deliberately no `bass808` block. Harmony is \"guitar-and-bass-led 4-chord cycles, acoustic-guitar arpeggios\" with \"a sung-plus-rapped double-lead structure\", hence the major families, the guitar timbre hint and a `call_response` melody. ⚠ Confidence is medium: the bass-led method, gear and studio lineage are sourced, but \"tempo/harmony are catalogue-derived\". ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `Db`, `G`, and the remaining values `C`, `Am`, `Dm`, together with all 5 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
